& [HACL_F001] is unsupported expected argument domains
  + [observed] twenty-five positive cases expected subjects outside the sole enum cantor admitted by runtime profile 0.1
  + [cause] corpus validation checked its own family and argument shape but did not reapply the frozen procedure schemas
  + [effect] raw positive accuracy ratios combine in-domain routing with impossible expected arguments and cannot be used as general accuracy claims
  + [containment] evidence and raw ratios remain unchanged while the completion review marks the methodological limitation
  + [repair] successor harness must pin the catalogue schema and reject incompatible expectations before execution
  + [status] is open_for_successor

& [HACL_F002] is caller-stimulus identity misbinding
  + [observed] thirteen out-of-domain prompts selected the intended procedure with subject cantor even though the requested subject was another faculty
  + [cause] subject enum forces cantor and host verification does not compare validated string arguments with normalized caller stimulus
  + [effect] a full run could query and articulate the wrong identity while carrying a schema-valid high-confidence call
  + [containment] calibration used route-only and reached neither Cantor nor llama.cpp
  + [repair] deterministic host grounding must precede admission and receive focused positive, punctuation, case, substring, cross-subject, and negative tests
  + [status] is open_for_source_preserved_correction

& [HACL_F003] is confidence interpretation
  + [observed] the thirteen mismatched calls ranged from 0.7183 through 0.9648 confidence
  + [lesson] learned confidence describes model routing behavior and does not establish semantic identity integrity
  + [repair] retain the threshold and add orthogonal deterministic grounding rather than recalibrating confidence downward
  + [status] is retained_design_constraint
